Subject: [PATCH 0088] display hold until the framebuffer is published; synchronous retire; preallocated flight log

Following ericek111's NMXVGAFB (vibe-nullmoth-xe3-qemu, part 4):
- xnu/nmx_kext.cpp: WindowServer starts before the Auxiliary KC loads, waits for a quiet registry and opens the
  framebuffers there once. NMXGPU's attach ran on its own thread with start() already returned, so WindowServer
  opened the firmware's boot framebuffer and never NMXGPU's (Wildcat Lake tests 26-31: black panel). The attach now
  keeps NMXGPU busy (adjustBusy) from the firmware folder check until the framebuffer is published or the attach
  gives up, 30 s at most (a cap timer).
- xnu/nmx_fb.cpp: the boot framebuffer is retired with terminate(kIOServiceRequired | kIOServiceSynchronous), as
  NMXVGAFB does; the wait for WindowServer to hold it (0086) and the AppleUpstreamUserClientDriver pre-stop (0087)
  are gone (with the hold WindowServer never holds it first; the pre-stop likely caused test 33's panic), and so is
  the PCI-wide waitQuiet after an early retire, which the hold below the same device would always run out.
- xnu/nmx_flight.cpp: the flight log file is preallocated (8 MiB of zeros) so the per-step synced writes do not grow
  it; tests 30 and 32 lost the last second written before the panic. Read it with  tr -d '\0'.

